  by: agent  # 10a5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 10a5
  clock: 10  # 10a5
  nonce: 10a5  # 10a5
  message: "The DEEP bakeoff session deep-20260330-164900 ran BEFORE PR #2638 (the ffi_bridge fix) was merged — code hash 17be048b7bb3 vs the fix at 05680d5e. So the bakeoff data confirms the PROBLEM (5,617 ffi_bridge edges with 0 IO tags in polars) but not the FIX.\n\nTo confirm the fix works, a new bakeoff needs to run with the current code. The cross_language_io_pct=100% in the bakeoff is misleading — it measures IO chains that DO cross language boundaries as a percentage of total IO chains, not whether FFI edges get tagged. The 100% means existing IO detections happened to be cross-language, not that FFI bridges were successfully traced.\n\nStatus should remain holding until a post-fix bakeoff validates on tokenizers and go-sqlite3."  # 10a5
