- op: discuss  # e2b9
  at: '2026-03-30T22:25:24Z'  # e2b9
  by: agent  # e2b9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e2b9
  clock: 13  # e2b9
  nonce: e2b9  # e2b9
  message: "Post-fix bakeoff (deep-20260330-182014) on go-sqlite3 and tokenizers: 116 cgo_bridge and 361 ffi_bridge edges still have 0 IO tags. This is EXPECTED — the fix adds these edge types to the traceable sets, but the FFI destinations (sqlite3_open, tokenizer ops) aren't stdlib IO primitives in the catalogs. The fix enables the pathway; it only produces IO tags when FFI targets ARE catalog primitives (e.g., Go→C fopen, Python→Rust std::fs::read).\n\nThe invariant 'IO boundary chains must be traceable through FFI bridges' IS now satisfied at the code level: tag_io_boundaries() and _trace_entry_points() both include cgo_bridge and ffi_bridge. Tests verify this. The bakeoff result confirms no regressions. Status remains holding — the fix is correct but produces no observable change in these particular repos because their FFI calls target non-IO functions."  # e2b9
