  message: "Investigated available repos in ~/ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/ for FFI→IO validation. Results: Pillow (Python+C) has 0 ffi_bridge edges — uses C extensions (Python C API), not ctypes/cffi/PyO3. glfw (Go+C) has cgo but C code is window/display management, not stdlib IO. gocryptfs has cgo but C code is crypto (OpenSSL). No available repo has the pattern needed: an FFI bridge edge (ctypes/cffi/PyO3/cgo) whose target C/Rust function calls stdlib IO (fopen/fread/socket/etc). The fix IS code-correct (unit tests verify cgo_bridge and ffi_bridge are traceable). Need a repo with explicit FFI→IO to validate end-to-end. Options: (1) user suggests/clones one, (2) create a synthetic test fixture."  # 6461
